# What keeps the old product name after the rename to Atlas (RENAME-ATLAS-1), read by
# scripts/rename_to_atlas.py and tests/test_atlas_rename.py. Everything else is renamed.
#   ## <group>: <reason>     starts a group; docs/plans/atlas-rename.md explains each one
#   file <glob>              the whole file keeps its bytes (its path is still renamed)
#   text <glob> <regex>      the spans the regex matches keep their text, in contents and paths
# Globs are fnmatch patterns on the renamed, repository-relative path (`*` crosses `/`).
# To rename a group later (its servers deleted, the website moved), delete its lines here and
# run scripts/rename_to_atlas.sh again.

## digitalocean: the DigitalOcean team account, its project and the keychain entries keep their names; the code finds them by name
text * "Proxy Index(?: \(copy\))?"
text * (?:[Pp]roject|into|outside|named|in|not|team:) Proxy Index\b
text * Proxy Index (?:project|team|DigitalOcean|Spaces archive)\b
text * "Proxy Index" team
text * (?<=ACCOUNT = )"proxy-index"
text * "account": "proxy-index"
text * account="proxy-index"
text * "proxy-index": Account\(
text * Account\(\s*"proxy-index"
text * --account[ =]proxy-index\b
text * \{"leftclick", "proxy-index"\}
text * \["proxy-index"(?=[,\]])
text * \bproxy-index (?:account|manager inventory|manager, before)\b
text * _not_proxy_index_
text * \bproxy-index inventory\b
text * <code>proxy-index</code>(?=, (?:both|never)\b)
text * leftclick\|proxy-index\b

## buckets: the Spaces bucket and its key keep their names (and the owner's local copy of the archive)
text * proxy-index-archive\b

## owner-machines: names on the owner's Mac and the Mac minis: SSH key files, launchd agents, log folders, the local checkout folder
text * ~/\.ssh/proxy-index-campaign(?:-staging)?\b
text * "proxy-index-campaign(?:-staging)?"
text * ~/Library/Logs/proxy-index-campaign\b
text * com\.proxy-index\.campaign-watch\b
text * com\.proxyindex\.browser-node\b
text * `proxy-index/`
text * \bproxy-index/\.state\b
text * Proxy reviews/proxy-index\b

## old-servers: paths and systemd unit names on the servers that run today (the London and staging managers, the worker image, the API server, onboarding servers); the new Canada server's setup uses the new names
text * /opt/proxy-index(?:-campaign|-worker)?\b
text * /run/proxy-index-worker\b
text * /etc/proxy-index\b
text * /var/lib/proxy-index-api\b
text * proxy-index-campaign-[\w@.%{}*$()-]*
text * proxy-index-(?:orchestrator|daily|db-analyze|calculate|onboarding)\b[\w@.%{}*$()-]*

## website: page paths, files and names of the Shifter website (its own repository); they change there first
text * (?<![\w.~$}/-])/proxy-index(?![\w-])
text * https?://(?:www\.)?shifter\.io/proxy-index(?![\w-])
text * (?:\b(?:src|scripts)/(?:[\w.\[\]-]+/)*|(?<![\w-])og/)proxy-index\b(?![-_])
text * \bProxyIndex\w+|\bproxyIndex\w+|\bproxy-index-home\.tsx\b
text * branch `proxy-index`

## external-repos: other repositories keep their names (the old, frozen API repository and the website's)
text * proxy-index-api\b
text * proxy-index-website\b

## format-ids: identifiers inside files that live outside the repository (the Spaces archive, formula copies on the managers, browser manifests, the browser hosts' release marker); new code must keep reading them
text * proxy-index-(?:hour-formula|best-hours|raw-day|browser-raw)\b
text * \.proxy-index-release\.json\b

## checksummed: applied schema and migration files; their bytes (comments included) are recorded or applied in the databases
file src/atlas/schema.sql
file src/atlas/migrate_v*.sql
file src/atlas/calculated/migrate_v*.sql
file tests/fixtures/schema_v*.sql
file api/internal/store/migrations/*.sql

## history: dated reports record what ran at the time, with the names of the time
file docs/reports/*

## rename-tooling: the rename itself names what it renames
file scripts/rename_to_atlas.*
file tests/test_atlas_rename.py
text tests/test_ci_gates.py proxy[-_]index
text tests/test_server_setup.py "proxy[-_]index" not in
file docs/plans/atlas-rename.md
